# J53 — Ready Map resumes as the primary workspace with a compact result
#
# Keyless and deterministic. It drives the real guided Map plan against the
# offline reference target, leaves the successful Map unresolved, navigates
# the embedded gallery, restarts, and proves that Summary, not the final
# module-recommender output, is the landing surface. An explicit choice is
# still required after restart.
name: Ready Map resume keeps Summary primary and result choice compact
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME COLORTERM=truecolor KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_DEVEX_PHASE_FIXTURE=1
launch:
wait-for: 25 CHOOSE A TARGET
submit: demo
wait-for: 120 PDF phase reference fixture loaded
submit: /full
wait-live-snap: 15 MAP · ROUTE | 1-map-route
keys: Enter
wait-live-snap: 10 MAP · MODULES | 1b-map-modules
# Keep the Map workload runtime-free on this keyless fixture by disabling the
# model-backed threat-model task, matching the canonical J21 flow.
keys: 5
wait: 1
keys: Enter
wait-for: 10 STEP 3 OF 3
keys: a
wait-live-snap: 90 SYSTEM SUMMARY | 2-compact-result
expect: Viewing Map
expect: RESULT READY
expect: Map ready
expect: SYSTEM SUMMARY
expect: Shift+Tab next phase
expect-not: Result · Recommend modules
ask: Does completed Map work leave the real Summary workspace dominant while one compact receipt with explicit actions remains visible?
# Workspace hydration can finish after the result receipt first renders and
# restore the captured composer mode. Exercise view keys only after the shell
# has reached its stable idle state, then converge from the live footer.
wait-for: 30 ○ idle
nav-mode:
keys: Tab
wait-live-snap: 10 DATA-FLOW DIAGRAM | 3-dfd-still-interactive
expect: RESULT READY
expect: DATA-FLOW DIAGRAM
ask: Can the operator inspect the DFD before accepting the successful result, without the receipt becoming modal?
# Phase pages are read-only projections, not progression gates. Shift+Tab must
# let the operator inspect later persisted projections while Map remains the
# current journey phase.
keys: BTab
wait-live-snap: 10 Viewing Scan | 3b-browse-scan
expect: Viewing Scan
expect: Map ● · Scan ○
expect: next required Map
keys: BTab
wait-live-snap: 10 Viewing Review | 3c-browse-findings
expect: Viewing Review
expect: FINDINGS · 6
expect: Map ● · Scan ○ · Review ○
expect: next required Map
ask: Can Shift+Tab open the findings page without falsely advancing the current journey beyond Map?
# Exit without resolving, then relaunch with the same operator home and target.
keys: Escape
wait: 1
type: quit
keys: Enter
wait: 3
# The offline demo uses a process-owned temporary target. Recover the exact
# target we just exercised so the second shell hydrates the same attempt.
shell: latest=$(find "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}" -path '*/kuzushi-demo/.kuzushi/v3/workflow/phase-attempts.jsonl' -mmin -10 -print 2>/dev/null | while read -r file; do printf '%s\t%s\n' "$(stat -f %m "$file")" "$file"; done | sort -nr | head -1 | cut -f2-); test -n "$latest" && printf '%s\n' "${latest%/.kuzushi/v3/workflow/phase-attempts.jsonl}" > @ART/demo-target
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME COLORTERM=truecolor KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch: --target "$(cat @ART/demo-target)"
wait-live-snap: 120 SYSTEM SUMMARY | 4-restart-summary
expect: Viewing Map
expect: RESULT READY
expect: Map ready
expect: SYSTEM SUMMARY
expect-not: Result · Recommend modules
ask: On restart, is Summary the deterministic Map landing page while the unresolved choice remains honest?
nav-mode:
keys: u
wait: 2
wait-live-snap: 15 SYSTEM SUMMARY | 5-selected-map
expect: Viewing Map
expect: SYSTEM SUMMARY
expect-not: RESULT READY
ask: After explicit Use Map, does only the receipt disappear while the accepted Map workspace remains in place?
